/-!
# The two surviving SL₂ and S₅ comparisons

`compared_linearTwo_of_source` and `compared_symmetricFive_of_source` turn the
actual irreducible B.5.1 row data into `ComparedCase` for the literal seed. Both
retain the full-moved-space hypothesis supplied independently by the comparison
assembly. The SL₂ branch retains its actual Sylow offender image and reduced
natural action. The S₅ branch proves order two by minimality and reconstructs
the marking of the original LA action.

The exhaustive case assembly belongs to `qt-b05-preliminary-source-comparison`;
these are the two row implications, not an independent assertion of B.5.9.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, B.5.9,
printed pp.107–108, cases (I) and (II).
-/
